Recommends: samba, samba-common-bin, smbclient, cifs-utils
Description: system tweaks for Linux Mint: maintenance, services, Samba, Firefox
 MintTweaks puts in one GTK 3 window the system chores that otherwise go
 through apt, systemctl, journalctl, smb.conf and Firefox policies.
 .
 It covers four areas: disk usage and cleanup (with a preview of what apt
 would remove, and careful removal of old kernels), systemd services with
 their journals and a boot analysis, complete Samba management with share
 and account administration, testparm validation and automatic backups, and
 a Firefox extension catalogue installed through the browser's own policy
 mechanism.
 .
 A Home page shows a read-only system summary and diagnostics: half-configured
 packages, broken dependencies, failed services, boot-time journal errors, disk
 usage, pending restarts and old kernels.
 .
 Privileged actions go through polkit, and every command is run as an argv
 list rather than through a shell.
